  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RWI China Program 2017-2022 - RWI China Program 2017-2018</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">RWI Kinaprogram 2017-2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RWI&apos;s China program focuses on strengthening Chinese academic institutions in Human Rights components and teaching.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">RWI:s &#x201d;Human Rights Capacity Development Programme in China&#x201d; f&#xf6;r perioden &#xe4;r i huvudsak ett samarbete med den akademiska sektorn.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the Raoul Wallenberg Institute of Human Rights and Humanitarian Laws Human Rights Capacity Development Programme for China is to strengthen institutions and networks for the promotion and protection of human rights, including gender equality, in China.  The interventions intended outcomes are: Outcome 1: Improved human rights education and engagement, including education for gender equality, by key Chinese academic institutions; Outcome 2: Improved capacity for research- based advocacy, including an inter-sectional perspective, amongst academics, civil society organisations (CSOs), disabled people&apos;s organisations (DPOs) and government officials. Due to the difficulties associated with the Foreign NGO Law and other developments elaborated upon in the Risk Assessment and Mitigation Plans submitted to Sida, the two other outcomes originally planned under the Programme were deprioritized since 2020, namely: Outcome 3: Institutionalisation of human rights education within the Chinese prosecution system, and Outcome 4: Improved implementation of gender sensitive juvenile justice mechanisms among justice sector stakeholders. Instead, a new outcome relating to &quot;Global China&quot; and its impacts on human rights and the environment was added to the Programme in 2020, namely: Outcome 5: Increased knowledge and more effective engagement addressing China&apos;s role in global and regional governance and multilateral issues related to human rights, the environment and sustainable development.</narrative>
  </description>
